# commands/

Source of truth for slash commands. OpenCode discovers this directory as
`.opencode/commands/`; `scripts/install.sh` links it into other agents' command
directories (e.g. `.claude/commands/`), so `/name` always resolves to the
brain's content.

## What's inside

| File       | Purpose                                                                 |
| ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `setup.md` | The `/setup` command — reads the repo, asks the operator questions, and generates or updates `AGENTS.md` |

Each `<name>.md` here becomes `/name` in connected agents. YAML frontmatter
fields (`description`, `agent`, `model`) are agent-specific; keep bodies
self-contained so they work when the brain is imported as `.opencode/`.

## Conventions

- One command per file, `kebab-case` file name (`release-notes.md` → `/release-notes`).
- `$ARGUMENTS` carries what the operator types after the command name.
- Write paths as brain-relative with fallbacks (see root `AGENTS.md`).

Note: this file is named `README` (without `.md`) because OpenCode registers
every `.md` file here as a command; `README.md` would expose a `/README`
command. `scripts/install.sh` also skips both forms when merging item-level.
